{"_v":3,"id":"martin-guerre-west-end-2026","cat":"west-end","cs":65.39,"rc":8,"bd":{"positive":3,"mixed":4,"negative":1},"rv":[{"cn":"Dominic Maxwell","o":"The Times (UK)","s":64,"b":"Mixed","t":1,"u":"https://www.thetimes.com/culture/theatre-dance/article/martin-guerre-is-too-confusing-to-be-another-les-mis-ld5pfrktp","d":"2026-10-21","q":"I’m glad I’ve seen Martin Guerre — but, definitive or not, I found it intriguing rather than devastating, skilful more than soulful."},{"cn":"Matthew Hemley","o":"The Stage","s":60,"b":"Mixed","t":1,"u":"https://www.thestage.co.uk/reviews/martin-guerre-review-old-vic-theatre-london-matthew-warchus","d":"2026-10-21","q":"While die-hard fans might not feel completely satisfied by this new version, it's still a treat to hear the score of this under-performed musical sung and played so intimately."},{"cn":"Tim Bano","o":"Time Out London","s":56,"b":"Mixed","t":1,"u":"https://www.timeout.com/london/theatre/martin-guerre-review","d":"2026-10-20","q":"But it is, simply, not a great musical."},{"cn":"Nick Curtis","o":"Evening Standard","s":46,"b":"Negative","t":1,"u":"https://www.standard.co.uk/culture/theatre/martin-guerre-at-the-old-vic-b1301716.html","d":"2026-10-21","q":"It plays out like a pacy, screamy folk-horror, but one that takes itself far too seriously."},{"cn":"Stuart King","o":"London Box Office","s":86,"b":"Rave","t":2,"u":"https://www.londonboxoffice.co.uk/news/post/martin-guerre-the-old-vic-review","d":"2026-10-21","q":"You betcha, without the tiniest soupçons of a doubt."},{"cn":"Alex Wood","o":"WhatsOnStage","s":82,"b":"Positive","t":2,"u":"https://www.whatsonstage.com/news/martin-guerre-review-a-compelling-case-for-a-musical-with-a-complicated-past_1735581/","d":"2026-10-21","q":"This trimmed-down revival makes a compelling case for a long-misunderstood work."},{"cn":"Anya Ryan","o":"London Theatre","s":63,"b":"Mixed","t":2,"u":"https://www.londontheatre.co.uk/reviews/martin-guerre-review-old-vic","d":"2026-10-21","q"